    "result": "Excellent! All tests are now passing. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\nI fixed 2 failing tests in the frai-core test suite by making minimal, focused changes to the source code:\n\n### 1. **Fixed APPROVAL_STATUSES export** (`/packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js`)\n   - **Problem**: The test imported `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available as part of the default export\n   - **Solution**: Added proper ES6 named exports alongside the existing default export\n   - **Impact**: All exports remain compatible with both import styles\n\n### 2. **Fixed toxicityMetric function** (`/packages/frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js`)\n   - **Problem**: The function signature was `toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms)` but it was being called with `(outputs, references)`, causing references to be incorrectly used as banned terms\n   - **Solution**: Changed the function signature to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references)` and made it always use `defaultBannedTerms` internally\n   - **Impact**: Toxicity now correctly evaluates against the default banned terms, not reference data\n\n## Test Results\n\u2705 **All 39 tests passing** (28 in frai-core, 11 in frai-gate)\n- Duration: 1.2 seconds\n- All public exports remain functional\n- No existing tests were modified or deleted",
